{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116512",
      "title": "Lazy Loading Entire Route Groups",
      "lectureOrder": 305,
      "videoOrder": 290,
      "sourceHash": "5419dde13bc6066db4abc28dc9e7e32637834642c08a70592a96fc0db9d71530",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.87,
          "end": 3.6,
          "en": "So you saw how you can switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 6.66,
          "en": "a single route to lazy loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.66,
          "end": 8.94,
          "en": "and how you can load a component lazily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.94,
          "end": 11.943,
          "en": "with that loadComponent property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.08,
          "end": 15.03,
          "en": "But of course here in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.03,
          "end": 16.56,
          "en": "it's not just this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.56,
          "end": 19.44,
          "en": "that would benefit from lazy loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.44,
          "end": 24.27,
          "en": "Instead, this tasks new route would also benefit from it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.27,
          "end": 27.24,
          "en": "And it's quite common that you might have multiple routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.24,
          "end": 30.213,
          "en": "that would benefit from being loaded lazily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.23,
          "end": 33.39,
          "en": "Now of course we could switch this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.39,
          "end": 35.31,
          "en": "but that would actually a bit harder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.31,
          "end": 39.78,
          "en": "because this canLeaveEditPage canDeactivate guard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.78,
          "end": 42.39,
          "en": "can't easily be outsourced from that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.39,
          "end": 46.86,
          "en": "since it needs the NewTaskComponent type reference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.86,
          "end": 49.92,
          "en": "So splitting this into a separate file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.92,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "without eagerly loading the component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 54.453,
          "en": "will be difficult.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.07,
          "end": 59.91,
          "en": "But thankfully it's also not a problem we have to deal with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.91,
          "end": 62.61,
          "en": "because instead of setting up lazy loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.61,
          "end": 64.77,
          "en": "on a per route level here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.77,
          "end": 67.05,
          "en": "it would make more sense to load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.05,
          "end": 71.19,
          "en": "the entire group of routes lazily in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.19,
          "end": 73.53,
          "en": "which we can also do by going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.53,
          "end": 76.293,
          "en": "to the main app.routes.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.37,
          "end": 82.08,
          "en": "And here, Angular actually gives you an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.08,
          "end": 87.08,
          "en": "to referring to the user routes as we're currently doing it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 90.33,
          "en": "because at the moment I'm importing these user routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.33,
          "end": 92.88,
          "en": "from my users.routes file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.88,
          "end": 95.55,
          "en": "And therefore of course this file gets loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.55,
          "end": 98.78999999999999,
          "en": "and all the code that's loaded in there gets loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.78999999999999,
          "end": 100.893,
          "en": "All is loaded eagerly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 102.84,
          "en": "To change this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.84,
          "end": 107.84,
          "en": "we have to replace this children property here in this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.15,
          "end": 111.393,
          "en": "with the loadChildren property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.35,
          "end": 114.39,
          "en": "So you can see the pattern here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.39,
          "end": 116.82,
          "en": "When the property starts with load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.82,
          "end": 120.45,
          "en": "like loadComponent did here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.45,
          "end": 122.7,
          "en": "we're talking about lazy loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.7,
          "end": 124.83,
          "en": "Now, however, with the goal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.83,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "of lazily loading multiple routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 130.473,
          "en": "and they offer multiple components at once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 136.23,
          "en": "So what we can do here now is again the find a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.23,
          "end": 138.123,
          "en": "as a value for loadChildren.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.2,
          "end": 141.69,
          "en": "And this function, just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.69,
          "end": 145.173,
          "en": "then wants the result of calling the import function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 149.55,
          "en": "And again, to import, we should pass the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.55,
          "end": 152.19299999999998,
          "en": "to the file we wanna load lazily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 157.263,
          "en": "So in this case, the path to this users.routes file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.25,
          "end": 160.773,
          "en": "I'll copy that and paste that in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.82,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "And then, just as before, you should call then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 169.56,
          "en": "and then actually return the result from that imported file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.56,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "so this routes array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 174.45,
          "en": "And that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.45,
          "end": 176.43,
          "en": "With that, it's now just important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.43,
          "end": 178.05,
          "en": "that you delete this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.05,
          "end": 180.3,
          "en": "Otherwise, even if you're not using it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.3,
          "end": 183.84,
          "en": "you are still importing that eagerly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.84,
          "end": 185.403,
          "en": "So we should remove that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.36,
          "end": 189.36,
          "en": "But with that, we're now loading the user routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.36,
          "end": 193.71,
          "en": "and all the things that are imported there lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.71,
          "end": 196.23,
          "en": "which is of course a way better approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.23,
          "end": 200.04,
          "en": "than doing it on a per route level in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.04,
          "end": 203.64,
          "en": "So if you save this, if you go back to the starting page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.64,
          "end": 205.8,
          "en": "and you clear your network tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.8,
          "end": 207.75,
          "en": "you'll see that if you click on a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.75,
          "end": 209.76,
          "en": "we're loading even more chunks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.76,
          "end": 213.69,
          "en": "because now we're loading all the lazily loaded code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.69,
          "end": 217.923,
          "en": "for this entire tasks feature and all the related routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.82,
          "end": 221.85,
          "en": "And that's there for how you wanna approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.85,
          "end": 224.34,
          "en": "routing based lazy loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.34,
          "end": 227.79,
          "en": "Identify the routes for which it makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.79,
          "end": 230.61,
          "en": "to lazy load their components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.61,
          "end": 234.24,
          "en": "and then see if you can maybe structure your apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 234.24,
          "end": 238.023,
          "en": "such that you can load entire groups of routes lazily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 242.61,
          "en": "With that in this application, we could now, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 242.61,
          "end": 246.3,
          "en": "of course also get rid of this lazy loading here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.3,
          "end": 249.84,
          "en": "because we essentially always end up on this route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 254.16,
          "en": "if we navigate to users slash some user id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.16,
          "end": 257.61,
          "en": "So lazy loading this actually makes no sense anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.61,
          "end": 260.28,
          "en": "and therefore here I will indeed go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.28,
          "end": 265.28,
          "en": "to the non lazy loaded approach, so to the eager loading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.57,
          "end": 270.57,
          "en": "And I'll also put the resolver here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.57,
          "end": 273.15999999999997,
          "en": "back into the task component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.14,
          "end": 276.27,
          "en": "simply because here for this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.27,
          "end": 279.33,
          "en": "that makes a bit more sense in my opinion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 279.33,
          "end": 282.82,
          "en": "Hence, we can also remove all the unused imports here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.09000000000003,
          "end": 289.14,
          "en": "and then go to the TasksComponent file and re-add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.14,
          "end": 291.663,
          "en": "and export the resolver here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.18,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "Now in the users.routes.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.22,
          "end": 300.813,
          "en": "we just also have to add that import to resolveUserTasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 302.13,
          "end": 304.5,
          "en": "With that, of course, the TasksComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 304.5,
          "end": 308.43,
          "en": "is loaded eagerly again in this user routes file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.43,
          "end": 312.69,
          "en": "but the overall file, as you just learned, is loaded lazily,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.69,
          "end": 314.85,
          "en": "and therefore, of course the TasksComponent in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 315.72,
          "end": 318.033,
          "en": "is also loaded lazily.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
